DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvmm__ppaaggee__rreennaammee() function removes a page from one object, and adds it
     to another at the given page index.  The page is added to the given ob‐
     ject, and is removed from the object that is currently associated with.
     If the page is currently on the cache queue it will be deactivated unless
     it is wired or unmanaged, in which case the deactivation will fail.  The
     entire page is marked as dirty after the move.

     The arguments to vvmm__ppaaggee__rreennaammee() are:

     _m           The page to move.

     _n_e_w___o_b_j_e_c_t  The object the page should be inserted into.

     _n_e_w___p_i_n_d_e_x  The page index into _n_e_w___o_b_j_e_c_t at which the new page should
                 be inserted.

